{
  "$comment": "THE FORGE (#EXP-1613; src/forge.ts, ecode-core forge.rs). The PR-tree primitives every provider offers (#NEW-36, the session playbook): a PR's base is ANY branch (`pr.open{base}`); `pr.list_by_base`; `pr.retarget`; `pr.mergeability` = a path-wise three-way merge of head and base over their merge base (clean | dirty + the conflicting paths); `pr.squash_merge` lands the merged tree as ONE commit `m<n>` on the base, then every live child of the merged PR is retargeted onto its base (EXP-324) and the merged head branch is deleted (never the default branch); `pr.merge_ordered` squash-merges several PRs in the given order, each its own transaction, and stops at the first refusal; `pr.close` (children stay); `pr.files` = head against the merge base; `branch.rebase_onto{branch, onto, upstream}` replays the commits after `upstream` onto `onto` as `r<n>` (a dirty child after its parent landed: upstream = the parent's `headSha`); `push` (fast-forward unless `force`). MODEL: a commit = {parent, changes: path → content | null (removed)}; a branch names a commit. A refusal = {code, reason} (contract forgeReason), the state unchanged, no events. Every step lists the events it emits (contract forgeEvent). `expect` = the branches, the PRs and the commits the case created, after the last step. Replayed by packages/ecode (bun test), apps/web/src/lib/ecode/ecode-spec.test.ts and ecode-core (cargo test); GithubForge and every Forge implementation conform to it.",
